 to <MATH_0004> is denoted\n<MATH_0005>\nThis makes sense since the pair defines a morphism into\n<MATH_0006> and we already have the structure\nmorphism into <MATH_0007> so combined we get a morphism into\n<MATH_0008>.\nVia Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe can identify <MATH_0009> with a relative Proj of\nthe graded <MATH_0010>-algebra <MATH_0011>\nand we can characterize <MATH_0012>\nas the unique <MATH_0013>-morphism such that\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nwhere we think of <MATH_0014> as a global section of\n<MATH_0015> via the map <MATH_0016> of\nLemma <REF_0003>; details omitted.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b81749c8a6f53a3212d90010ebc0f596ee16bd035b95c2af9d397157dc9c1d80", "unit_id": "tag:01ND:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01ND", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$n$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$n + 1$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\mathbf{P}^n_{\\mathbf{Z}} =\n\\bigcup\\nolimits_{i = 0, \\ldots, n} D_{+}(T_i)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D_{+}(T_i)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathbf{A}^n_{\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0007": "$n$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathbf{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-standard-covering-projective-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e0abea476d5d832219b993eee9a6cb9c4e40eb173ce132f5f7b7fcbc080f6fd4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f1745017f7b255dfc6d2b7491a6c03b703b7bdef68e42a852822bda43c455d93", "source_text": "Projective <MATH_0001>-space over <MATH_0002> is covered by\n<MATH_0003> standard opens\n<MATH_0004>\nwhere each <MATH_0005> is isomorphic to <MATH_0006>\naffine <MATH_0007>-space over <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:88f36b0f5ddcc733c9e8d1318d26cd9c0537cf45d4213040724837c3cb91c96d", "unit_id": "tag:01NG:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01ND", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{Z}[T_0, \\ldots, T_n]_{+} = (T_0, \\ldots, T_n)$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\Spec\n\\left(\n\\mathbf{Z}\n\\left[\\frac{T_0}{T_i}, \\ldots, \\frac{T_n}{T_i}\n\\right]\n\\right)\n\\cong\n\\mathbf{A}^n_{\\mathbf{Z}}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4b069500cffde9c2f5a574de70490a4ab14c0680341202fd04888c6cbe62ec7f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:69ed491b0da2dc6bb1846ffabc0756b9b86d8d6d392b9164141fef209b85aa36", "source_text": "This is true because\n<MATH_0001> and\nsince\n<MATH_0002>\nin an obvious way.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d664a3727b2bef70f57a7e505cbbd00665aa49f10f37c90c47ae2cf7a06a702e", "unit_id": "tag:01NG:proof"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01ND", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{P}^n_S \\to S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-projective-space-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e7298305bf8cecf71a543fdf43dbafb0b6f6fe2556383b0f4c83fa65870869e0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:61bbff667f39423c3ed43aa2ad931d59cf373cd05b039182392f972d961b322a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nThe structure morphism <MATH_0002> is\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> separated,\n<STRUCT_0003> quasi-compact,\n<STRUCT_0004> satisfies the existence and uniqueness parts of the valuative criterion,\nand\n<STRUCT_0005> universally closed.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:94b450f69683cb25b42e9e766fee3120952e43d48eec1bd02fd3d963e1f257b2", "unit_id": "tag:01NH:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01ND", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{P}^n_{\\mathbf{Z}} \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-separated-permanence}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-proj-separated}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-standard-covering-projective-space}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-proj-valuative-criterion}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{schemes-proposition-characterize-universally-closed}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:34f3075bc89f25d2374657c95561b9f9adcf850c1a834c506d498f050e4a714c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:368d67961d42aab94decf3b655ca363edb709a0f011d5462bd5a4e4f88ed6f5e", "source_text": "All these properties are stable under base change (this is clear for the\nlast two and for the other two see\nSchemes, Lemmas\n<REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>).\nHence it suffices to prove them for the morphism\n<MATH_0001>.\nSeparatedness is Lemma <REF_0003>. Quasi-compactness follows\nfrom Lemma <REF_0004>.\nExistence and uniqueness of the valuative criterion follow from\nLemma <REF_0005>.\nUniversally closed follows from the above and\nSchemes, Proposition <REF_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7feedd44de1d8cc1ca99aaf27a51254b4197507ac3a71cb8163efcb2f492db3c", "unit_id": "tag:01NH:proof"}
